1
00:00:11,670 --> 00:00:13,300
The city gates close
at curfew every day.

2
00:00:13,728 --> 00:00:15,670
Why are you demanding
a special pass tonight?

3
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:17,760
(Zhengyang Gate)
I'm just following orders.

4
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:20,510
It's not my place
to question my superiors.

5
00:00:21,350 --> 00:00:23,000
If I let you through,

6
00:00:23,136 --> 00:00:24,440
and they hold me responsible,

7
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:25,920
even with ten lives,

8
00:00:26,048 --> 00:00:27,000
I couldn't pay for it.

9
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:28,760
Unless...

10
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:30,030
Unless what?

11
00:00:30,390 --> 00:00:32,640
Unless you bring me an official order

12
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:34,210
=Cases Between Us=
from the Police Department

13
00:00:34,224 --> 00:00:35,750
or a higher authority revoking the pass.

14
00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:38,500
=Episode 35=

15
00:00:38,520 --> 00:00:39,880
What's the holdup?

16
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:41,280
Commander Yuan.

17
00:00:44,016 --> 00:00:45,920
Director Wang
from the Administration Office

18
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,070
will be here in ten minutes.

19
00:00:47,070 --> 00:00:47,710
Yang Dezhi,

20
00:00:48,070 --> 00:00:49,640
if you still want to stay as a Chief,

21
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:51,200
take your men and leave.

22
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:53,880
So you're moving
the shipment tonight.

23
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:55,840
What did I tell you
back at the camp?

24
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:58,030
Interfere with
military business again,

25
00:00:58,110 --> 00:00:59,470
and I won't go easy on you.

26
00:01:00,150 --> 00:01:01,430
You think I'm joking?

27
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:04,230
You framed my father with this,

28
00:01:05,216 --> 00:01:08,208
then sold the shipment
to Westerners. How much are you making?

29
00:01:09,510 --> 00:01:11,070
That's none of your concern.

30
00:01:24,230 --> 00:01:26,040
That's a police-issued sidearm.

31
00:01:26,112 --> 00:01:28,784
Do you want everyone to face
disciplinary action because of you?

32
00:01:28,950 --> 00:01:30,480
I still wanted to believe

33
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:33,000
you had no choice.

34
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:35,790
I was too naive.

35
00:01:46,710 --> 00:01:48,510
Are they still
surrounding the gate?

36
00:01:48,510 --> 00:01:49,280
Yes.

37
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:51,950
Yuan Hong is holding them there.

38
00:01:51,950 --> 00:01:53,120
A brilliant move, sir.

39
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:55,070
Using Zhao Shaoshang as bait.

40
00:01:55,070 --> 00:01:56,310
He took it.

41
00:01:57,560 --> 00:01:59,680
Yuan Hong's always suspicious.

42
00:02:01,070 --> 00:02:02,840
But once you've got Zhao Shaoshang,

43
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:04,480
he'll walk right into the trap.

44
00:02:05,430 --> 00:02:06,480
The British said

45
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:08,630
the treasures would be exchanged
for German weapons,

46
00:02:08,630 --> 00:02:10,430
shipment by shipment.

47
00:02:11,030 --> 00:02:12,310
Stay sharp.

48
00:02:12,310 --> 00:02:12,910
Yes, sir.

49
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:37,430
What's happening up ahead?

50
00:02:37,750 --> 00:02:38,870
I'll go take a look.

51
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:41,960
Run!

52
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:58,030
Taking the treasure out of the city
in the middle of the night?

53
00:03:58,112 --> 00:03:59,630
Quite a thrill, isn't it, Secretary Xu?

54
00:04:02,590 --> 00:04:04,590
What game are you playing,
Commander Yuan?

55
00:04:04,590 --> 00:04:05,870
A diversion.

56
00:04:05,870 --> 00:04:07,590
You played a fine game.

57
00:04:09,030 --> 00:04:10,310
I'm afraid

58
00:04:10,310 --> 00:04:11,630
I don't know what you mean.

59
00:04:25,824 --> 00:04:27,488
Commander, they're national treasures.

60
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:30,360
Trafficking national treasures,

61
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:32,070
and framing an innocent man.

62
00:04:32,430 --> 00:04:33,830
You've got some nerve.

63
00:04:35,872 --> 00:04:36,680
Commander Yuan,

64
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:39,000
are you here to avenge Zhao Shaoshang,

65
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:41,510
or to steal the prize yourself?

66
00:04:46,950 --> 00:04:49,600
Looks like the weapons
were too tempting.

67
00:04:50,270 --> 00:04:51,240
Does Zhao Shaoshang

68
00:04:51,750 --> 00:04:53,800
know how heartless you are?

69
00:04:54,430 --> 00:04:56,750
You climb the ranks

70
00:04:57,190 --> 00:04:58,560
at the expense of his family.

71
00:04:59,160 --> 00:04:59,870
I have to say,

72
00:04:59,870 --> 00:05:01,800
you're truly your father's son.

73
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:03,830
Your father betrayed your mother.

74
00:05:04,310 --> 00:05:05,920
You betrayed your best friend.

75
00:05:05,984 --> 00:05:07,616
The apple doesn't fall
far from the tree.

76
00:05:12,656 --> 00:05:13,984
Take those imperial antiques.

77
00:05:15,630 --> 00:05:17,040
Am I wrong?

78
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:19,750
Or...

79
00:05:19,750 --> 00:05:20,480
don't you know

80
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:22,070
what your father did to your mother?

81
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:24,630
Or maybe you've guessed,

82
00:05:25,190 --> 00:05:26,680
but you're too afraid to face it.

83
00:05:26,880 --> 00:05:27,750
Isn't that right?

84
00:05:30,310 --> 00:05:31,390
Take him, too.

85
00:05:31,920 --> 00:05:32,800
Keep him alive.

86
00:05:33,190 --> 00:05:33,750
Yes, sir.

87
00:05:37,660 --> 00:05:40,420
(Map)

88
00:05:40,430 --> 00:05:41,310
Come in.

89
00:05:45,392 --> 00:05:47,800
Marshal, Young Marshal
intercepted the antiques at the docks.

90
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:49,750
The British arms ship has withdrawn.

91
00:05:51,390 --> 00:05:52,600
Well done.

92
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:58,600
Chen thought he could outfox me.

93
00:05:58,950 --> 00:06:00,870
He overestimated himself.

94
00:06:01,310 --> 00:06:02,070
However,

95
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:03,310
Young Marshal

96
00:06:03,310 --> 00:06:04,750
kept Secretary Xu behind.

97
00:06:08,720 --> 00:06:11,120
Send an urgent telegram
to Kobayashi.

98
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:11,880
Tell him

99
00:06:12,560 --> 00:06:13,830
we have those imperial antiques.

100
00:06:14,750 --> 00:06:16,430
Proceed as planned.

101
00:06:17,270 --> 00:06:17,920
Yes, sir.

102
00:06:18,680 --> 00:06:19,390
Marshal,

103
00:06:20,270 --> 00:06:21,270
shouldn't we play it safe

104
00:06:21,270 --> 00:06:22,480
and get rid of Secretary Xu?

105
00:06:24,390 --> 00:06:25,600
No need.

106
00:06:26,830 --> 00:06:28,600
They're all expendable.

107
00:06:29,310 --> 00:06:30,070
Do not

108
00:06:31,160 --> 00:06:32,680
alert the enemy.

109
00:06:39,630 --> 00:06:40,430
Easy.

110
00:06:40,430 --> 00:06:42,160
Ten lives wouldn't be enough
to pay for it.

111
00:06:44,190 --> 00:06:44,920
Careful.

112
00:06:53,360 --> 00:06:54,190
Move out.

113
00:06:54,190 --> 00:06:55,560
We leave the city before dawn.

114
00:07:07,950 --> 00:07:09,600
I've detained Kobayashi's men.

115
00:07:09,808 --> 00:07:10,920
Go collect the shipment.

116
00:07:12,750 --> 00:07:14,920
Someone will meet you at the warehouse.

117
00:07:15,950 --> 00:07:16,800
What about you?

118
00:07:17,390 --> 00:07:20,190
There are some scores
I need to settle in person.

119
00:07:21,580 --> 00:07:22,980
(Faithful to Duty)

120
00:07:29,072 --> 00:07:30,720
Adjutant, an urgent telegram comes in.

121
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:32,410
Mr. Kobayashi wants the shipment
taken to the docks.

122
00:07:32,420 --> 00:07:33,070
By water instead.

123
00:07:33,070 --> 00:07:34,360
Wasn't it already shipped?

124
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:38,920
This is bad.

125
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:39,920
Men!

126
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:40,750
Come with me.

127
00:07:46,128 --> 00:07:48,080
Why are you in such a hurry,
Adjutant Sun?

128
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:48,870
Where are you going?

129
00:07:53,070 --> 00:07:53,800
Young Master,

130
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:57,720
are you really turning
against the Marshal?

131
00:07:57,720 --> 00:07:59,190
That's quite an accusation.

132
00:07:59,950 --> 00:08:01,830
My enemy is those foreigners.

133
00:08:02,070 --> 00:08:03,720
Also, my father said it himself.

134
00:08:03,950 --> 00:08:06,000
Recover every last item.

135
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,240
I did exactly that.

136
00:08:07,480 --> 00:08:09,560
I simply returned them to their owner.

137
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:12,680
To their owner?

138
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:14,430
Men!

139
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:15,680
Tie him up!

140
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:27,160
What are you waiting for?

141
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:28,070
Didn't you hear me?

142
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:31,510
Last time,

143
00:08:31,510 --> 00:08:33,440
I caught you dealing with the Japanese.

144
00:08:33,440 --> 00:08:34,840
You forced me back into the army.

145
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:38,150
Isn't this all about making me
fall out with my father?

146
00:08:38,390 --> 00:08:40,320
Your plan came together sooner
than expected.

147
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:41,550
Why are you panicking?

148
00:08:46,510 --> 00:08:47,550
Jizhi.

149
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:50,720
My replacement?

150
00:08:52,320 --> 00:08:53,960
What a fitting name.

151
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:57,080
You wanted to be my father's son.

152
00:08:57,720 --> 00:09:00,440
In the end, you're just his dog.

153
00:09:03,750 --> 00:09:04,630
Look around.

154
00:09:07,910 --> 00:09:09,120
No one dares to touch me.

155
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:30,870
Marshal.

156
00:09:33,320 --> 00:09:34,750
My good son.

157
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:36,720
You've barely been back,

158
00:09:36,720 --> 00:09:38,630
and you're already staging a mutiny?

159
00:09:41,870 --> 00:09:44,150
Where did you send my shipment?

160
00:09:44,150 --> 00:09:45,270
Every last piece

161
00:09:45,510 --> 00:09:46,630
went back to its owner.

162
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:48,440
You deceived your superiors,

163
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:49,750
twisted my orders,

164
00:09:50,030 --> 00:09:51,840
and now you've got a death wish?

165
00:09:51,840 --> 00:09:52,360
What?

166
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:53,960
First my mother,

167
00:09:53,960 --> 00:09:55,360
and now me?

168
00:09:56,672 --> 00:09:58,320
What nonsense are you talking about?

169
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:00,670
Do you know

170
00:10:00,670 --> 00:10:02,510
I've been lying to myself
all these years?

171
00:10:02,750 --> 00:10:03,750
When my mother died,

172
00:10:03,750 --> 00:10:06,120
you wouldn't even give her
a proper funeral.

173
00:10:06,510 --> 00:10:08,550
I told myself it was because
you never loved her.

174
00:10:08,550 --> 00:10:09,720
But the truth

175
00:10:10,510 --> 00:10:11,720
is horrific.

176
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:12,840
I can't believe

177
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:14,750
you'd use her life as a bargaining chip!

178
00:10:14,750 --> 00:10:15,600
Tell me!

179
00:10:16,630 --> 00:10:18,150
Did you use her life to cover up

180
00:10:18,870 --> 00:10:20,192
the Japanese selling radium drinks

181
00:10:20,224 --> 00:10:23,080
and trading it
for two shiploads of weapons?

182
00:10:31,510 --> 00:10:32,080
Did Xu

183
00:10:32,080 --> 00:10:34,600
tell you all this?

184
00:10:36,360 --> 00:10:37,550
You did it.

185
00:10:38,320 --> 00:10:39,670
Why deny it now?

186
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:42,750
You moron.

187
00:10:42,750 --> 00:10:43,870
Back when Chen and I

188
00:10:43,870 --> 00:10:45,750
faced off for months in Baoding,

189
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:47,960
do you know why they did this?

190
00:10:47,960 --> 00:10:49,870
To drive a wedge between us,

191
00:10:49,870 --> 00:10:51,630
so they could exploit the rift.

192
00:10:51,630 --> 00:10:52,390
How could you

193
00:10:52,390 --> 00:10:54,120
fall into their trap

194
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:55,200
so easily?

195
00:10:55,200 --> 00:10:57,270
Don't you have any
sense of the bigger picture?

196
00:11:01,670 --> 00:11:03,080
So you admit it.

197
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:12,720
It was an accident.

198
00:11:13,030 --> 00:11:15,000
When your mother fell ill,

199
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:15,960
I was desperate, too.

200
00:11:15,960 --> 00:11:17,240
I sought every doctor I could.

201
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:19,200
But nothing could save her.

202
00:11:19,510 --> 00:11:20,720
When I learned the truth,

203
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:22,320
I confronted Kobayashi.

204
00:11:22,840 --> 00:11:24,200
He said he didn't know either.

205
00:11:24,440 --> 00:11:25,510
He also said

206
00:11:25,510 --> 00:11:26,790
he felt deeply sorry.

207
00:11:26,790 --> 00:11:29,120
He compensated me with
two shiploads of weapons.

208
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:29,960
An accident?

209
00:11:31,750 --> 00:11:32,960
And you expect me

210
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:34,390
to buy such a childish excuse?

211
00:11:41,630 --> 00:11:43,550
Even if it was deliberate, so what?

212
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:45,200
What could we have done?

213
00:11:45,510 --> 00:11:47,630
The Japanese Army was behind them!

214
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:49,600
The Japanese Army!

215
00:11:50,550 --> 00:11:51,670
Could we beat them?

216
00:11:53,550 --> 00:11:55,200
No matter how much
I loved your mother,

217
00:11:55,200 --> 00:11:57,630
could I gamble

218
00:11:57,630 --> 00:11:58,870
my men's lives?

219
00:11:59,320 --> 00:12:00,510
You're not me.

220
00:12:00,790 --> 00:12:02,200
You can't understand.

221
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:06,720
This is the first time

222
00:12:07,008 --> 00:12:09,120
I've seen someone make
selling out his own wife

223
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:10,750
sound so noble.

224
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:13,630
Marshal.

225
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:16,910
Don't think that just
because you're my son,

226
00:12:16,910 --> 00:12:18,840
I won't shoot you.

227
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:19,720
Go ahead!

228
00:12:20,030 --> 00:12:21,630
If anything happens to me today,

229
00:12:22,120 --> 00:12:23,480
by tomorrow morning,

230
00:12:23,870 --> 00:12:25,960
the headlines will expose

231
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:27,872
how you sold out your wife
to the Japanese.

232
00:12:29,080 --> 00:12:30,630
Let's find out

233
00:12:31,910 --> 00:12:33,320
what the people think

234
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:36,960
of their patriotic general.

235
00:12:50,550 --> 00:12:51,150
Fine.

236
00:12:52,870 --> 00:12:54,320
For defying orders

237
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:57,630
and insulting a superior,

238
00:12:58,320 --> 00:13:00,670
lock him up immediately.

239
00:13:00,870 --> 00:13:02,480
If he won't admit he's wrong,

240
00:13:02,600 --> 00:13:04,720
keep him there for the rest of his life!

241
00:13:04,870 --> 00:13:05,630
Yes, sir.

242
00:13:08,816 --> 00:13:10,320
My mother's death remains unavenged.

243
00:13:10,832 --> 00:13:12,752
Our nation has yet to erase
its humiliation.

244
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:15,750
I'm ashamed to be your son.

245
00:14:25,720 --> 00:14:26,840
Where are you going?

246
00:14:28,150 --> 00:14:29,960
That shipment at the Weng City...

247
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:30,750
Don't go.

248
00:14:31,472 --> 00:14:32,910
You don't need to look into it.

249
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:35,390
What do you mean?

250
00:14:51,630 --> 00:14:52,630
What's going on?

251
00:14:52,630 --> 00:14:54,120
Someone sent me a message last night.

252
00:14:54,120 --> 00:14:56,000
It said the Marshal's mistress,
Madam Yuan,

253
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:57,904
died after drinking
a Japanese radium tonic.

254
00:14:57,952 --> 00:14:59,390
Not only did the Marshal cover it up,

255
00:14:59,390 --> 00:15:01,670
but he also traded it
to the Japanese for weapons.

256
00:15:01,670 --> 00:15:02,510
The letter told me

257
00:15:02,510 --> 00:15:04,150
to wait for a call at the newspaper.

258
00:15:04,150 --> 00:15:06,550
If no call came before dawn,

259
00:15:06,550 --> 00:15:08,030
I'd publish the story.

260
00:15:08,320 --> 00:15:09,270
If I did as instructed,

261
00:15:09,270 --> 00:15:10,630
I would find the imperial antiques

262
00:15:10,630 --> 00:15:11,600
and save Father.

263
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:13,440
I had no better option,

264
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:15,030
so I took a chance.

265
00:15:15,030 --> 00:15:17,200
Before dawn, the phone rang.

266
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:19,600
It was our East Suburb warehouse.

267
00:15:19,790 --> 00:15:22,150
They said our shipment had arrived

268
00:15:22,150 --> 00:15:23,870
and insisted I inspect it.

269
00:15:23,870 --> 00:15:25,150
When I got there,

270
00:15:25,480 --> 00:15:26,750
I saw Yang Dezhi.

271
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:28,630
Chief stayed in the army

272
00:15:28,704 --> 00:15:30,980
because he knew about the Marshal's deal
with the Japanese

273
00:15:30,992 --> 00:15:32,480
and wanted to get to the bottom of it.

274
00:15:32,480 --> 00:15:34,390
He never expected
your family to be framed

275
00:15:34,390 --> 00:15:35,910
and dragged into all this.

276
00:15:35,910 --> 00:15:37,150
So he could only risk his life

277
00:15:37,550 --> 00:15:39,390
to save you.

278
00:15:45,030 --> 00:15:46,550
Yuan Hong wrote the letter.

279
00:15:47,240 --> 00:15:48,510
Wan'er, take the shipment

280
00:15:48,510 --> 00:15:50,270
and the thumb ring
to the police station.

281
00:15:50,750 --> 00:15:51,600
Zhao Cai.

282
00:15:51,960 --> 00:15:52,960
Let's go.

283
00:15:58,150 --> 00:15:59,080
(Heaven, please.)

284
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:00,600
(Don't let anything happen.)

285
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:17,200
You must be Young Master Zhao.

286
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:21,510
You know me?

287
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:28,000
The famous Young Master Zhao in Beijing.

288
00:16:28,440 --> 00:16:30,390
Who doesn't

289
00:16:31,080 --> 00:16:32,960
know you?

290
00:16:33,870 --> 00:16:36,440
It's an honor to finally meet you.

291
00:16:36,630 --> 00:16:38,510
You're quite

292
00:16:38,510 --> 00:16:40,000
the handsome gentleman.

293
00:16:40,390 --> 00:16:42,320
No wonder

294
00:16:42,320 --> 00:16:43,550
my son insisted

295
00:16:43,550 --> 00:16:45,320
on hanging around with you.

296
00:16:47,670 --> 00:16:48,720
Cut the crap.

297
00:16:49,240 --> 00:16:50,270
Release Yuan Hong.

298
00:16:51,750 --> 00:16:54,440
Looks like your safety is still on.

299
00:16:54,960 --> 00:16:56,120
Shut up!

300
00:16:56,120 --> 00:16:57,320
Release Yuan Hong!

301
00:16:59,120 --> 00:17:00,510
Stay put! Put the gun down!

302
00:17:05,480 --> 00:17:06,640
What are you doing here?

303
00:17:07,640 --> 00:17:08,340
To save you.

304
00:17:08,350 --> 00:17:09,070
Are you blind?

305
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:10,590
Untie him.

306
00:17:21,070 --> 00:17:22,160
Untie him.

307
00:17:22,160 --> 00:17:22,750
Marshal.

308
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:23,880
Untie him!

309
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:25,000
Now!

310
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:26,200
Let him go.

311
00:17:32,350 --> 00:17:33,750
Tell your men to lower their guns.

312
00:17:33,750 --> 00:17:35,000
Lower your guns.

313
00:17:38,240 --> 00:17:39,030
Get a car ready.

314
00:17:39,030 --> 00:17:40,000
We're leaving.

315
00:17:43,240 --> 00:17:44,510
Did you hear me?

316
00:17:51,830 --> 00:17:53,440
Do as he says.

317
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:54,240
Marshal.

318
00:17:54,510 --> 00:17:56,550
Do as he says.

319
00:17:56,550 --> 00:17:57,350
Yes, sir.

320
00:18:15,960 --> 00:18:17,310
Why did you come?

321
00:18:19,888 --> 00:18:21,510
Yuan Hong, can you talk like a human

322
00:18:21,510 --> 00:18:22,400
for once?

323
00:18:23,488 --> 00:18:24,640
Next time you shove me away

324
00:18:24,640 --> 00:18:25,776
and play the hero again,

325
00:18:25,792 --> 00:18:27,216
I'll slap the crap out of you!

326
00:18:27,510 --> 00:18:29,000
If I didn't come, who would bury you?

327
00:18:30,750 --> 00:18:32,030
You?

328
00:18:32,640 --> 00:18:34,160
Without his approval,

329
00:18:34,550 --> 00:18:36,400
you'd never have seen him,

330
00:18:36,400 --> 00:18:38,720
let alone pointed a gun at his head.

331
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:39,590
Yeah.

332
00:18:41,070 --> 00:18:43,240
Father and son put on quite a show.

333
00:18:43,370 --> 00:18:45,340
One willing to hit,
the other willing to take it.

334
00:18:45,504 --> 00:18:48,240
And you dragged me and
all your father's loyal men into it.

335
00:18:52,240 --> 00:18:52,960
I'm sorry.

336
00:18:57,030 --> 00:18:57,590
Thank you.

337
00:19:05,060 --> 00:19:08,140
(End of Episode 35)

338
00:19:09,880 --> 00:19:11,520
